BEGIN:VEVENT
IMAGE;VALUE=URI;DISPLAY=BADGE;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org
 /wp-content/uploads/2026/07/FFPRS-tinaCardona-August2026.jpg
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://inprinthouston.org/wp-content/uploads/202
 6/07/FFPRS-tinaCardona-August2026.jpg
UID:PFHfZ0xGdjwbEJoh8yTDq
SUMMARY:First Fridays Presents Tina Cardona
DTSTAMP:20260806T110908Z
DTSTART:20260807T193000Z
DESCRIPTION:Free and open to the public \nDoors @ 7 pm\nPop-up poet @ 7:30 
	pm\nFeatured poet @ 7:40 pm\nOpen mic @ 8:15 pm \nInprint is proud to serv
	e as the host for the First Fridays Reading Series. The First Fridays Read
	ing Series is the oldest poetry series in Houston and was organized by Rob
	ert Clark from 1975-2019. Today\, First Fridays events are curated and hos
	ted by local community members. \nThe August featured reader will be Tina 
	Cardona\, a community maker for Houston poets as a co-founder of hotpoet.o
	rg. She is a psychotherapist\, yoga teacher\, earth advocate\, dog guardia
	n\, soothsayer\, mother and partner\, and is also in a long-standing\, con
	flictual relationship with poetry. You can find her wandering at dawn and 
	at dusk muttering with trees. \nThe opening pop-up poet will be Michael J.
	 Galko\, a retired scientist and active poet from Houston. He is the artis
	t responsible for ‘haiku house’\, a residential art installation consistin
	g of hundreds of original wood-burned and painted haiku. He was a finalist
	 in the 2020 Naugatuck River Review and the 2022 Bellevue Literary Review 
	poetry contests. Recent poems appear in Spillway Magazine\, Atlanta Review
	\, Silk Road Review\, and Plainsongs\, among other journals. \nFor more in
	formation about the First Fridays Reading Series\, click here. To join the
	 First Fridays Facebook group\, click here. \n\n\nhttps://inprinthouston.o
	rg/event/first-fridays-presents-tina-cardona-2/\n\nFrom Inprint Houston
URL:https://inprinthouston.org/event/first-fridays-presents-tina-cardona-2/
LOCATION:Inprint House\, 1520 W Main St\, Houston\, TX\, 77006\, United Sta
	tes
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:inprint-houston
CATEGORIES:Inprint Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT2H
END:VEVENT
